1. Object-Oriented Programming Core Concepts

 * Class (The Engineering Drawing): A blueprint written once that defines how to construct objects.
 * Object / Instance (The Physical Part): A specific machine or part built from that drawing. One drawing can produce many independent instances, each with its own state.
 * Attributes (What the Machine Has): Variables attached to an object that store its state (e.g., tag name, max RPM, current speed, parts made).
 * Methods (What the Machine Does): Functions defined inside a class that operate on the object's attributes.


