4. Demystifying self

 * Definition: self represents "which specific machine are we talking about?"
 * How It Works: When calling L1.make_part(), Python automatically passes L1 as the first argument (self).
 * Isolation Guarantee: Writing self.parts_made += 1 inside a method increments only that specific machine's counter and leaves other instances untouched.
5. Key Takeaways
 * Constructor (__init__): Runs automatically whenever a new object is created to set up its initial attributes.
 * State Isolation: Every instance built from a class maintains its own distinct data in memory—modifying L1 will never accidentally alter L2.
